COPY public.boxingposts (id, fight_id, hook, caption, visualtext, cta, tone, source_summary, status, reviewer_note, hook_template_id, model, generated_at, approved_at, published_at, created_at, updated_at) FROM stdin;
9436ead9-a852-4999-a17c-508001b4d521	6a3ab496-a075-4b00-99c8-252a28f19319	IBF Heavyweight gold on the line, and half of Britain thinks Wardley got gifted his ticket here.	Dubois rolls in 22-2 with 21 KOs and that Joshua starching still fresh — but he's been dropped himself, and the Usyk knockdowns left questions about his nerve. Wardley is unbeaten at 18-0-1 with 16 stoppages, yet earned this off a split-decision many call a robbery. Power meets pressure, and someone's reputation breaks in London.	Gifted shot or hidden killer?	Wardley shocker or Dubois KO — call the round in the comments.	provocative	David Wardley faces Daniel Dubois for the IBF Heavyweight Championship on September 13, 2026, at Tottenham Hotspur Stadium in London. Wardley enters undefeated at 18-0-1 with 16 knockouts, having earned the mandatory shot via a controversial split-decision win. Dubois holds a 22-2 record with 21 knockouts and arrives off a knockout victory over Anthony Joshua. The fight pits a hometown underdog against a heavy-favorite power-puncher who has himself been dropped, notably against Usyk. No result or finishing round has been recorded.	published	Strong hook. Approved for Friday slot.	dde6851c-ca02-485f-bb9f-c5c51c28908a	claude-opus-4-8	2026-06-22 21:56:29.595477+00	2026-06-22 21:58:59.776228+00	2026-06-22 21:59:20.635483+00	2026-06-22 21:56:29.595477+00	2026-06-22 21:59:20.570379+00
c4140c5d-6b76-437d-9ce1-a86047091ae8	759ffceb-e59c-42bc-a7b0-696b76c0ce3f	Two unbeaten 'Monsters', 47 combined knockouts, one nation holding its breath — and only one walks out undisputed.	Inoue brings 28-0 with 25 KOs; Nakatani answers with 29-0 and 22 stoppages of his own. This isn't a tune-up — it's the fight Japan has built toward for two years, with pound-for-pound supremacy and the entire Super Bantamweight crown on the line at the Tokyo Dome. Nakatani's size and reach are real problems, but Inoue's finishing instinct in the clutch may be the difference.	Two Monsters. One throne.	Who's getting his hand raised — Inoue or Nakatani — and in what round? Drop it below.	hyped	Naoya Inoue (28-0, 25 KO) is scheduled to face Junto Nakatani (29-0, 22 KO) for the Undisputed Super Bantamweight championship on December 31, 2026, at the Tokyo Dome in Tokyo. Both fighters are unbeaten at world level, and the matchup carries pound-for-pound implications. The event is projected to be the first Japanese boxing pay-per-view to outsell Mayweather-Pacquiao domestically, and is described as the bout Japanese boxing has been building toward for two years. The result and any knockout round are not yet known.	rejected	Test rejection.	0d146ce0-a27e-41cd-bfd4-3a0fb6c63cb6	claude-opus-4-8	2026-06-22 21:59:53.850635+00	\N	\N	2026-06-22 21:59:53.850635+00	2026-06-22 22:00:24.578119+00
